prompt:
Please review the open pull request in `pr/2788/` for this account service. Read the diff alongside the surrounding implementation, tests, configuration, and documentation, then decide whether I should merge it. This is close to release, and I need findings grounded in behavior and in promises the project already makes to its users. Call out defects that could affect users or make the change unsafe, and distinguish merge blockers from smaller issues. Do not assume that a passing test proves the contract is preserved. Write the review to `REVIEW.md` at the top of the project. End the review with a fenced `json` list of findings, each containing `location` (`path/to/file.ext:LINE`, with line numbers of the file as it is in the project), `severity` (`critical`, `high`, `medium`, `low` or `nit`), `issue`, and `fix`.

```json
[
  { "location": "path/to/file.ext:LINE", "severity": "medium", "issue": "what is wrong and why it matters", "fix": "an actionable correction" }
]
```
